<title>JAPAN: Shionogi starts clinical test of HIV drug in U.S.</title>
<headline>Shionogi starts clinical test of HIV drug in U.S.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shionogi and Co Ltd said on Thursday that it started clinical trials in the United States earlier this month of an HIV drug made from imidazole derivatives.</p>
<p>In previous in vitro tests, the drug showed significant effectiveness in suppressing the human immunodeficiency virus when used in combination with other HIV drugs, including AZT, the firm said in a statement.</p>
<p>Shionogi said it will consider conducting clinical trials in Japan after the first phase of the three-stage testing in the United States is completed.</p>
</text>
